            "Status": "preferred",
            "Explanation": "One of Linji Yixuan's four named selections: the member whose wording says that both the person and the encountered scene are taken away. Linji's own record places it after taking away only the person and taking away only the scene, and before taking away neither; the four are roster alternatives, not a report of two physical objects disappearing. In Eyes of Humans and Gods, a reviewed unnamed monk asks Linji about this member, and Linji answers with news from Bing and Fen being cut off and one quarter standing alone. Later reviewed unnamed monks ask Yuanwu Keqin, Feiyin Tongrong, and Jie'an Wujin the same public question. Yuanwu answers \u2018gather in,\u2019 paired with \u2018let out\u2019 for taking away neither; Feiyin asks where the questioner can establish a body; Jie'an answers once that deliberation is a thousand miles away and elsewhere orders the questioner to take a beating twice. Tianyin Yuanxiu quotes Linji's complete four-member roster and publicly asks which member Tianyin's own shout enacts. These named responses preserve a recurring public question and a Linji-house selection, but their incompatible answers do not supply one hidden definition of person or scene.",
            "Validation": "multi-source",
            "Note": "The exact headword occurs 168 times in 99 allowlisted texts. The longer variant with an added \u2018both\u2019 occurs 327 times in 123 texts and remains family evidence, not a second sense. Direct roster declaration, public question, short answer, paired opposite, body question, beating command, and later shout test all retain one named selection. Seven exact witnesses from six source texts exceed the frequency floor without using family material as depth.",
